Consumption__Follow_up_Generator;
Equipment list
Inventory list
Logistic report – Narrative
Fleet Management report
Water consumption report
Supply Chain Management:
SFU (Pharmacy, Buffer stock, NFI warehouse)
IKD_Follow-Up
CFU
Supply Plan(Monthly Update)
Monitor logistics and supply indicators and analyse them.
Position Requirements
A Bachelor Degree in Business Administration OR Logistics OR Purchasing and Supply
Master`s Degree in Business Administration OR Logistics OR Purchasing and Supply preferred;
Min 3 years’ extensive experience in Logistics and Supply Chain Management, preferably in Humanitarian or development work
Certification in Supply or Logistics desirable (CIPS, CILT, etc);
High level of Integrity and Transparency;
Capacity to conduct trainings and team management;
Computer literacy including all Microsoft Office programs (Word, Excel, Power point);
Excellent attention to detail, highly organized, rigorous, self-motivated, strong sense of responsibility, ability to work independently;
Capacity for analysis, synthesis and reporting of large amounts of information;
High level of Integrity and Transparency;
Excellent people management skills combined with the ability and desire to further develop staff capacity;
Possess strong analytical, communication, interpersonal and negotiation skills;
Effective multi-tasking skills with ability to coordinate and handle pressure/ stress well;
Flexible, able to live and work in a stressful and insecure environment;
Previous experience working for NGOs an asset, particularly international.

