To be qualified for the position of a Senior Lecturer (CONUASS 5), the candidate must have:
A Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D) degree;
At least three (3) years fulltime teaching experience as a Lecturer I (however a candidate with two (2) years full time experience as a Lecturer I and outstanding publications in Q1 and Q2 journals may be considered);
A minimum of twenty-seven(27)points, of which sixteen (16) points must be from recognized peer review journals. Six (6) out of the 16 points must be obtained from publications in reputable journals indexed in Thompson Reuters (Clarivate Analytics) or Scopus;
A Google Scholar h-index of at least 2; and
Evidence of full professional registration with relevant professional bodies (where applicable).
